<title>ARGENTINA: Argentina, Brazil to invest $2.0 bln in road works.</title>
<headline>Argentina, Brazil to invest $2.0 bln in road works.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentina and Brazil will invest $2.0 billion in road works to facilitate the trasportation of merchandise between them, La Nacion newspaper said Wednesday.</p>
<p>The investment plan &quot;Maestro&quot; seeks investments of $700 million by Argentina and $1.3 billion by Brazil to repair and build new roads, especially at border crossings.</p>
<p>It will be announced during a meeting in Brazil between Presidents Carlos Menem of Argentina and Fernando Henrique Cardoso of Brazil on April 26, La Nacion said.</p>
<p>Argentina and Brazil are the main parters of the customs union Mercosur, which also includes Paraguay and Uruguay.</p>
<p>Last year, their bilateral trade soared to $12 billion from $5.0 billion in 1993.</p>
<p>((-- Patrick Adam, Buenos Aires Newsroom 541 318-0654))</p>
